  "@type": "RecordSpecification",
  "sharedVocabulary": {
    "@ref": "./shared.vocabulary.jsonld",
    "description": "References common field definitions, types, and patterns"
  },
  "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
  "name": "Flight Leg Record (Record Type 3)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "specType": "core",
  "description": "The Flight Leg Record (RT3) contains the core flight schedule data for a single flight leg (a non-stop segment from origin to destination). It specifies carrier, flight number, operating period, days of operation, departure/arrival stations and times, aircraft type, booking classes, and various operational details. RT3 records follow their parent RT2 (Carrier) record and may be followed by RT4 (Segment Data) records.",
  "aiNotes": "The Flight Leg Record (RT3) is the heart of SSIM - it defines individual flights.\n\nKey Concepts:\n\n**Flight Leg**: A single non-stop flight segment (e.g., SYD→LAX). A multi-leg journey like SYD→DXB→LHR consists of TWO RT3 records.\n\n**Critical Fields**:\n1. **Flight Identity**: airline_designator + flight_number (e.g., 'QF ' + '0001')\n2. **Routing**: departure_station → arrival_station (e.g., 'SYD' → 'LAX')\n3. **Timing**: aircraft_std/sta (departure/arrival times)\n4. **Schedule**: period_of_operation_from/to + days_of_operation\n5. **Aircraft**: aircraft_type (e.g., '388' = A380-800)\n6. **Booking**: passenger_reservations_booking_designator (cabin classes)\n\n**Hierarchical Structure**:\nRT1 (Header) → RT2 (Carrier) → **RT3 (Flight Leg)** → RT4 (Segment Data)\n\n**Time Mode Inheritance**:\nRT3 times are interpreted using time_mode from parent RT2:\n- time_mode='L': Times are LOCAL to each airport\n- time_mode='U': Times are UTC\n\n**Days of Operation**:\n7-character string where each position represents a day:\n- Position 1 = Monday\n- Position 2 = Tuesday\n- ...\n- Position 7 = Sunday\n- '1234567' = Operates all 7 days\n- '1 3 5 7' = Operates Mon, Wed, Fri, Sun\n- '      7' = Operates Sunday only\n\n**Common Workflows**:\n\n1. **Schedule Loading**:\n   - Parse RT2 (get carrier, time_mode, validity period)\n   - Parse RT3 records (individual flights)\n   - Parse RT4 records (segment details)\n   - Load into booking system\n\n2. **Flight Search**:\n   - Query by departure_station + arrival_station\n   - Filter by days_of_operation\n   - Check period_of_operation_from/to\n   - Return matching flights\n\n3. **Multi-leg Itinerary**:\n   - RT3 #1: SYD→DXB (leg_sequence_number=01)\n   - RT3 #2: DXB→LHR (leg_sequence_number=02)\n   - Same flight_number, different leg_sequence_number\n\n**Important Validations**:\n- period_of_operation must be within RT2 validity window\n- Either passenger_reservations_booking_designator OR aircraft_configuration_version must be present (not both blank)\n- departure_station ≠ arrival_station\n- aircraft_sta typically > aircraft_std (but not always - day crossing!)\n\n**Use Cases**:\n- Flight schedule management\n- Booking system integration\n- Flight search and availability\n- Crew scheduling\n- Aircraft rotation planning\n- Passenger notifications\n- Operational planning",
  "iataChapter": "7.5.3",
  "iataVersion": "2025.35",
  "recordType": 3,
  "metadata": {
    "encoding": {
      "allowed": [
        "ASCII",
        "EBCDIC"
      ],
      "ascii": {
        "blank_hex": "0x20",
        "zero_hex": "0x30"
      },
      "ebcdic": {
        "blank_hex": "0x40",
        "zero_hex": "0xF0"
      }
    },
    "statusLegend": {
      "M": "Mandatory",
      "C": "Conditional",
      "O": "Optional"
    },
    "conventions": {
      "positions": "Byte positions are 1-based and inclusive",
      "padding": "Unless noted, blanks are used to pad unused bytes",
      "fill_rules": {
        "blank": "Fill with space characters",
        "zero": "Fill with numeric zeroes"
      },
      "alignment": {
        "left": "Left-justify content; pad on the right",
        "right": "Right-justify content; pad on the left"
      }
    }
  },
  "codec": {
    "@type": "Codec",
    "codecType": "fixed_width",
    "length": 200,
    "byteOrder": "big-endian",
    "encoding": "ASCII",
    "recordTerminator": null,
    "notes": "All SSIM records are exactly 200 bytes. RT3 follows RT2 and precedes RT4 records for this flight leg."
  },
  "fields": [
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#record_type",
      "name": "record_type",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 0,
        "end": 0,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": true,
      "constantValue": "3",
      "status": "M",
      "description": "Record type identifier. Always '3' for Flight Leg records.",
      "aiNotes": "Record type discriminator. Always '3' for Flight Leg records. Use for parser routing.",
      "validation": {
        "type": "constant",
        "value": "3"
      },
      "examples": [
        "3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#operational_suffix",
      "name": "operational_suffix",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 1,
        "end": 1,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "fillRule": "blank",
      "description": "Operational suffix for the flight. Blank when not used. Used to distinguish operational variants of the same flight number.",
      "aiNotes": "Optional operational suffix. Distinguishes variants of same flight.\n\nExample: Flight AA100 might have:\n- AA100 (no suffix) = Normal operation\n- AA100A (suffix='A') = Alternative routing\n- AA100B (suffix='B') = Seasonal variant\n\nUsually blank. When used, single alpha character.",
      "examples": [
        " ",
        "A",
        "B"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#airline_designator",
      "name": "airline_designator",
      "fieldType": "iata_airline",
      "position": {
        "start": 2,
        "end": 4,
        "length": 3
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[A-Z0-9]{2}[A-Z0-9 ]$",
      "description": "IATA airline code. Must match the airline_designator from the parent RT2 record. 2-3 alphanumeric characters, left-justified.",
      "aiNotes": "Operating carrier code. Should match parent RT2 airline_designator.\n\nFormat:\n- 2-char codes: 'QF ', 'AA ', 'DL ' (note trailing space!)\n- 3-char codes: 'UAL'\n\nThis is the OPERATING carrier (airline actually flying the aircraft).\nFor code-share flights, see operating_airline_disclosure_marker.",
      "examples": [
        "QF ",
        "AA ",
        "DL ",
        "BA ",
        "UAL"
      ],
      "relatesTo": {
        "@type": "FieldRelationship",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2#airline_designator",
        "relationship": "must_match",
        "description": "Must match airline from parent RT2 record"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#flight_number",
      "name": "flight_number",
      "fieldType": "flight_number",
      "position": {
        "start": 5,
        "end": 8,
        "length": 4
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[ 0-9A-Z]{1,4}$",
      "alignment": "right",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Flight number. Right-justified, blank-padded. May be numeric (most common) or alphanumeric.",
      "aiNotes": "Flight number. Format: Right-justified, blank-padded to 4 chars.\n\nExamples:\n- '   1' = Flight 1\n- '  12' = Flight 12\n- ' 450' = Flight 450\n- '1234' = Flight 1234\n- ' 12A' = Flight 12A (rare alphanumeric)\n\nRange: Typically 1-9999, but can include letters.\n\nDisplay: Remove leading blanks ('   1' → '1')\n\nCombined with airline_designator forms unique flight identity:\n'QF ' + ' 001' = QF001 (Qantas Flight 1)",
      "examples": [
        "   1",
        "  12",
        " 450",
        "1234",
        " 12A"
      ],
      "relatesTo": {
        "@type": "FieldRelationship",
        "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#airline_designator",
        "relationship": "forms_flight_identity_with",
        "description": "airline_designator + flight_number = unique flight identity"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#itinerary_variation_identifier",
      "name": "itinerary_variation_identifier",
      "fieldType": "integer",
      "position": {
        "start": 9,
        "end": 10,
        "length": 2
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "zeroPad": 2,
        "radix": 10
      },
      "range": {
        "min": 0,
        "max": 99
      },
      "description": "Itinerary variation identifier (00-99). Groups different routing variations for the same flight number. Value 00 indicates default/no variation.",
      "aiNotes": "Variation ID for different routings of same flight number.\n\nExample: QF1 (daily service, multiple routings):\n- Variation 00: Default/primary routing (common in practice)\n- Variation 01: SYD→SIN→LHR (via Singapore)\n- Variation 02: SYD→DXB→LHR (via Dubai)\n\nSame flight number (QF1), different itineraries.\n\nFormat: Zero-padded 2 digits (00-99)\n\nMost flights: '00' or '01' (only one routing)\n\nValue '00' found in production SSIM files from major carriers (UA, B6) - indicates default/no variation.\n\nUsed when:\n- Seasonal route changes\n- Alternative routings\n- Day-specific variations",
      "examples": [
        "00",
        "01",
        "02",
        "15",
        "99"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#leg_sequence_number",
      "name": "leg_sequence_number",
      "fieldType": "integer",
      "position": {
        "start": 11,
        "end": 12,
        "length": 2
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "zeroPad": 2,
        "radix": 10
      },
      "range": {
        "min": 0,
        "max": 99
      },
      "description": "Leg sequence number (00-99) within the itinerary variation. For multi-leg flights, increments sequentially. Value 00 indicates default/single leg.",
      "aiNotes": "Sequence number for multi-leg flights.\n\nSingle-leg flight:\n- Leg 00: Default/single leg (found in production)\n- Leg 01: SYD→LAX (direct)\n\nMulti-leg flight (QF1):\n- Leg 01: SYD→SIN\n- Leg 02: SIN→LHR\n\nBoth legs have same flight_number ('QF1') but different leg_sequence_number.\n\nFormat: Zero-padded 2 digits (00-99)\n\nMost flights: '00' or '01' (single leg)\n\nValue '00' found in production SSIM files from major carriers (UA, B6) - indicates default/single leg.\n\nMaximum: 99 legs (theoretical, rarely exceeds 5)\n\nSequence must be monotonic (00, 01, 02, 03...)",
      "examples": [
        "00",
        "01",
        "02",
        "03",
        "10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#service_type",
      "name": "service_type",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 13,
        "end": 13,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "description": "Service type code. Indicates the type of service (passenger, cargo, etc.).",
      "aiNotes": "Service type indicator. Values found in production SSIM files:\n\n**Common values:**\n- 'J' = Passenger Jet (most common - 6.5M+ records per carrier)\n- 'F' = Freight/Cargo (13-16k records)\n- 'C' = Charter Passenger (13-15k records)\n- 'P' = Positioning flight (500-600 records)\n- 'U' = Unknown/Unscheduled (270-280k records)\n\n**Additional values (found in UA, B6, WS production data):**\n- 'V' = Charter Cargo or Van/Vehicle service (18-20k records)\n- 'G' = General Aviation (14-15k records)\n- 'S' = Surface/Bus (RFS - Road Feeder Service) (600-700 records)\n- 'Q' = Queue/Special service (700-800 records)\n- 'H' = Helicopter service (160-180 records)\n- 'O' = Other service (100-400 records)\n- 'A' = Additional service (3-160 records)\n- 'L' = Long-haul or other variant (4-100 records)\n- 'M' = Mail service (16-20 records)\n- 'K', 'E', 'T', 'R' = Other specialized services (<50 records each)\n\nProduction data note:\nAll values A-Z found in United Airlines (UA), JetBlue (B6), and WestJet (WS) SSIM files. Most common is 'J' (passenger jet) accounting for ~95% of flights, followed by 'U' (unknown/unscheduled) at ~4%.\n\nAffects:\n- Passenger bookability\n- Regulatory requirements\n- Operational handling\n- Aircraft type and configuration",
      "examples": [
        "J",
        "F",
        "P",
        "C",
        "U",
        "V",
        "G",
        "S",
        "Q",
        "H",
        "O",
        "A",
        "L",
        "M",
        "K",
        "E",
        "T",
        "R"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#period_of_operation_from",
      "name": "period_of_operation_from",
      "fieldType": "ssim_date",
      "position": {
        "start": 14,
        "end": 20,
        "length": 7
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "dateFormat": "DDMMMYY"
      },
      "description": "Start date of flight operation. Format: DDMMMYY. Must fall within the RT2 carrier validity period. Interpreted according to parent RT2 time_mode.",
      "aiNotes": "Flight operation start date. Format: DDMMMYY\n\nMust be within parent RT2 period_of_validity_from/to.\n\nExample:\n- RT2 validity: 01JAN24 to 31MAR24\n- RT3 operation: 15JAN24 to 28FEB24 ✓ Valid (within RT2 window)\n- RT3 operation: 01DEC23 to 15JAN24 ✗ Invalid (starts before RT2)\n\nInterpretation: Uses RT2 time_mode (U=UTC, L=Local)\n\nDay-of-week application: Applied to aircraft_std (departure time)",
      "examples": [
        "07DEC24",
        "01JAN25",
        "15MAR24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#period_of_operation_to",
      "name": "period_of_operation_to",
      "fieldType": "ssim_date",
      "position": {
        "start": 21,
        "end": 27,
        "length": 7
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "dateFormat": "DDMMMYY"
      },
      "description": "End date of flight operation. Format: DDMMMYY. Must fall within the RT2 carrier validity period. Special value: '00XXX00' indicates indefinite operation (no end date).",
      "aiNotes": "Flight operation end date. Format: DDMMMYY\n\nStandard format:\n- DD: Day (01-31)\n- MMM: Month code (JAN, FEB, MAR, APR, MAY, JUN, JUL, AUG, SEP, OCT, NOV, DEC)\n- YY: Year (00-99, with Y2K logic: 00-49 = 2000-2049, 50-99 = 1950-1999)\n\nSpecial value '00XXX00' (IATA SSIM convention):\n- Indicates indefinite operation (no end date)\n- Flight operates from period_of_operation_from with no planned end\n- Commonly used for seasonal or ongoing routes\n- Parser returns time.Time{} (zero value) which can be checked with IsZero()\n\nMust be:\n- ≥ period_of_operation_from (if not XXX)\n- Within parent RT2 period_of_validity_to (if not XXX)\n\nDefines inclusive operation period with period_of_operation_from.\n\nCombined with days_of_operation determines exact operating dates.",
      "examples": [
        "02FEB25",
        "31MAR25",
        "30JUN24",
        "00XXX00"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#days_of_operation",
      "name": "days_of_operation",
      "fieldType": "day_mask",
      "position": {
        "start": 28,
        "end": 34,
        "length": 7
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[1-7 ]{7}$",
      "description": "Days of operation within the period. 7-character mask where each position represents a day (1=Monday...7=Sunday). Blank = no operation, digit = operates. Applied to aircraft_std.",
      "aiNotes": "Days of week the flight operates. Format: 7-character string.\n\nPosition mapping:\n- Position 1 = Monday ('1' or ' ')\n- Position 2 = Tuesday ('2' or ' ')\n- Position 3 = Wednesday ('3' or ' ')\n- Position 4 = Thursday ('4' or ' ')\n- Position 5 = Friday ('5' or ' ')\n- Position 6 = Saturday ('6' or ' ')\n- Position 7 = Sunday ('7' or ' ')\n\nExamples:\n- '1234567' = Daily (Mon-Sun)\n- '12345  ' = Weekdays only (Mon-Fri)\n- '     67' = Weekends only (Sat-Sun)\n- '1 3 5 7' = Mon, Wed, Fri, Sun\n- ' 2 4 6 ' = Tue, Thu, Sat\n- '      7' = Sunday only\n\nBlank = No operation that day\nDigit = Operates that day\n\nApplied to: aircraft_std (departure time)\n\nDate calculation:\nFor each date in [period_of_operation_from, period_of_operation_to]:\n  if day_of_week matches days_of_operation:\n    Flight operates on this date",
      "examples": [
        "1234567",
        "12345  ",
        "     67",
        "1 3 5 7",
        "      7"
      ],
      "decode": {
        "as": "array",
        "itemBytes": 1,
        "stripBlanks": true,
        "itemPattern": "^[1-7]$"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#frequency_rate",
      "name": "frequency_rate",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 35,
        "end": 35,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "fillRule": "blank",
      "description": "Frequency rate indicator. Blank when not used. Rarely used field for irregular frequency patterns.",
      "aiNotes": "Frequency rate (rarely used). Usually blank.\n\nFor special frequency patterns not captured by days_of_operation.\n\nMost schedules: Blank (use days_of_operation instead)",
      "examples": [
        " "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#departure_station",
      "name": "departure_station",
      "fieldType": "iata_airport",
      "position": {
        "start": 36,
        "end": 38,
        "length": 3
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[A-Z]{3}$",
      "description": "3-letter IATA airport code for departure. Must be different from arrival_station.",
      "aiNotes": "Departure airport. Format: 3-letter IATA code (uppercase).\n\nExamples:\n- 'SYD' = Sydney Kingsford Smith\n- 'LAX' = Los Angeles International\n- 'DXB' = Dubai International\n- 'LHR' = London Heathrow\n\nValidation:\n- Must be valid IATA airport code\n- Must ≠ arrival_station (no zero-length legs!)\n\nUsed for:\n- Flight search\n- Airport operational planning\n- Passenger information\n- Slot management",
      "examples": [
        "SYD",
        "LAX",
        "JFK",
        "LHR",
        "DXB"
      ],
      "relatesTo": {
        "@type": "FieldRelationship",
        "target": "iata.airport",
        "relationship": "references_airport",
        "description": "Links to IATA airport registry"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#passenger_std",
      "name": "passenger_std",
      "fieldType": "time",
      "position": {
        "start": 39,
        "end": 42,
        "length": 4
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "timeFormat": "HHMM"
      },
      "pattern": "^(?:[01][0-9]|2[0-3])[0-5][0-9]$",
      "description": "Passenger Scheduled Time of Departure (STD). Format: HHMM (24-hour). Nearly always equals aircraft_std but must be completed. Interpreted according to RT2 time_mode and departure_utc_variation.",
      "aiNotes": "Passenger departure time. Format: HHMM (24-hour)\n\nExamples:\n- '0830' = 08:30 (8:30 AM)\n- '1430' = 14:30 (2:30 PM)\n- '2359' = 23:59 (11:59 PM)\n\nTypically equals aircraft_std.\n\nWhen different:\n- Passenger check-in closes before aircraft departure\n- Passenger boarding vs aircraft pushback\n\nMost cases: passenger_std = aircraft_std\n\nInterpretation:\n- If RT2 time_mode='L': Local time at departure_station\n- If RT2 time_mode='U': UTC time\n\nUse departure_utc_variation for timezone offset",
      "examples": [
        "0830",
        "1430",
        "2350",
        "0000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#aircraft_std",
      "name": "aircraft_std",
      "fieldType": "time",
      "position": {
        "start": 43,
        "end": 46,
        "length": 4
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "timeFormat": "HHMM"
      },
      "pattern": "^(?:[01][0-9]|2[0-3])[0-5][0-9]$",
      "description": "Aircraft Scheduled Time of Departure (STD). Format: HHMM (24-hour). This is the official departure time used for scheduling and operational purposes. Interpreted according to RT2 time_mode and departure_utc_variation.",
      "aiNotes": "Aircraft departure time (official). Format: HHMM (24-hour)\n\nThis is THE departure time for:\n- Schedule planning\n- Slot allocation\n- Crew scheduling\n- Aircraft rotation\n- Day-of-operation calculation\n\ndays_of_operation is applied to THIS time.\n\nExample:\nFlight operates Mon-Fri ('12345  ')\naireraft_std = '2350' (23:50)\nDeparture day: Monday 23:50\n\nInterpretation depends on RT2 time_mode:\n- time_mode='L': Local time at departure airport\n- time_mode='U': UTC time\n\nUse departure_utc_variation for UTC offset.",
      "examples": [
        "0830",
        "1430",
        "2350",
        "0000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#departure_utc_variation",
      "name": "departure_utc_variation",
      "fieldType": "utc_offset",
      "position": {
        "start": 47,
        "end": 51,
        "length": 5
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[+-][0-9]{4}$",
      "description": "UTC offset at departure station. Format: ±HHMM (e.g., +1000, -0500). Indicates hours and minutes offset from UTC. See SSIM Appendix F.",
      "aiNotes": "Departure airport UTC offset. Format: ±HHMM\n\nExamples:\n- '+1000' = UTC+10:00 (Sydney AEDT)\n- '+0800' = UTC+08:00 (Singapore, Hong Kong)\n- '+0000' = UTC (London GMT)\n- '-0500' = UTC-05:00 (New York EST)\n- '-0800' = UTC-08:00 (Los Angeles PST)\n\nSign:\n- '+' = East of UTC (ahead)\n- '-' = West of UTC (behind)\n\nHHMM:\n- HH = Hours (00-14)\n- MM = Minutes (00, 30, 45 typically)\n\nUses:\n1. Convert local to UTC\n2. Calculate day crossing\n3. Time zone display\n\nExample:\nLocal time: 23:50 (departure_station=SYD)\nUTC offset: +1000\nUTC time: 13:50 (previous day!)\n\nNote: Offset can change with DST! Schedule may need adjustment.",
      "examples": [
        "+1000",
        "+0800",
        "+0000",
        "-0500",
        "-0800",
        "+0930"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#departure_terminal",
      "name": "departure_terminal",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 52,
        "end": 53,
        "length": 2
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Passenger terminal at departure airport. Left-justified, blank-padded. Conditional field (blank if not used).",
      "aiNotes": "Departure terminal. Format: 2 characters, left-justified.\n\nExamples:\n- 'I ' = International Terminal\n- 'D ' = Domestic Terminal\n- '1 ' = Terminal 1\n- 'T3' = Terminal 3\n- 'A ' = Terminal A\n\nBlank if:\n- Airport has only one terminal\n- Terminal not specified\n- Not applicable\n\nUsed for:\n- Passenger information\n- Ground transportation\n- Connecting flight guidance",
      "examples": [
        "I ",
        "D ",
        "1 ",
        "T3",
        "A ",
        "  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#arrival_station",
      "name": "arrival_station",
      "fieldType": "iata_airport",
      "position": {
        "start": 54,
        "end": 56,
        "length": 3
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[A-Z]{3}$",
      "description": "3-letter IATA airport code for arrival. Must be different from departure_station.",
      "aiNotes": "Arrival airport. Format: 3-letter IATA code (uppercase).\n\nExamples:\n- 'LAX' = Los Angeles\n- 'DXB' = Dubai\n- 'SIN' = Singapore\n\nMust ≠ departure_station\n\nCombined with departure_station defines the route:\n'SYD' → 'LAX' = Sydney to Los Angeles route",
      "examples": [
        "LAX",
        "DXB",
        "SIN",
        "LHR",
        "JFK"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#aircraft_sta",
      "name": "aircraft_sta",
      "fieldType": "time",
      "position": {
        "start": 57,
        "end": 60,
        "length": 4
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "timeFormat": "HHMM"
      },
      "pattern": "^(?:[01][0-9]|2[0-3])[0-5][0-9]$",
      "description": "Aircraft Scheduled Time of Arrival (STA). Format: HHMM (24-hour). Official arrival time. Interpreted according to RT2 time_mode and arrival_utc_variation.",
      "aiNotes": "Aircraft arrival time (official). Format: HHMM (24-hour)\n\nExamples:\n- '0600' = 06:00 (6:00 AM)\n- '1430' = 14:30 (2:30 PM)\n\nInterpretation depends on RT2 time_mode:\n- time_mode='L': Local time at arrival airport\n- time_mode='U': UTC time\n\nDay crossing:\nIf aircraft_sta < aircraft_std, flight crosses midnight!\n\nExample:\nDeparture: 2350 (23:50)\nArrival: 0600 (06:00)\n→ Arrives next day\n\nUse arrival_utc_variation for UTC offset.",
      "examples": [
        "0600",
        "1430",
        "2359",
        "0000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#passenger_sta",
      "name": "passenger_sta",
      "fieldType": "time",
      "position": {
        "start": 61,
        "end": 64,
        "length": 4
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "timeFormat": "HHMM"
      },
      "pattern": "^(?:[01][0-9]|2[0-3])[0-5][0-9]$",
      "description": "Passenger Scheduled Time of Arrival (STA). Format: HHMM (24-hour). Nearly always equals aircraft_sta. Interpreted according to RT2 time_mode.",
      "aiNotes": "Passenger arrival time. Format: HHMM (24-hour)\n\nTypically equals aircraft_sta.\n\nWhen different:\n- Passenger deplaning time vs aircraft parking\n- Immigration/customs considerations\n\nMost cases: passenger_sta = aircraft_sta",
      "examples": [
        "0600",
        "1430",
        "2359"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#arrival_utc_variation",
      "name": "arrival_utc_variation",
      "fieldType": "utc_offset",
      "position": {
        "start": 65,
        "end": 69,
        "length": 5
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[+-][0-9]{4}$",
      "description": "UTC offset at arrival station. Format: ±HHMM (e.g., +0800, -0700). Indicates hours and minutes offset from UTC.",
      "aiNotes": "Arrival airport UTC offset. Format: ±HHMM\n\nSame format as departure_utc_variation.\n\nCan differ from departure_utc_variation:\n- Cross-timezone flights\n- Different DST rules\n\nExample (SYD→LAX):\n- departure_utc_variation: +1000 (Sydney)\n- arrival_utc_variation: -0800 (LA)\n- Time zone difference: 18 hours",
      "examples": [
        "+0800",
        "-0800",
        "+0000",
        "-0500"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#arrival_terminal",
      "name": "arrival_terminal",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 70,
        "end": 71,
        "length": 2
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Passenger terminal at arrival airport. Left-justified, blank-padded. Conditional field (blank if not used).",
      "aiNotes": "Arrival terminal. Format: 2 characters, left-justified.\n\nSame format as departure_terminal.\n\nUsed for:\n- Connecting flight information\n- Ground transportation\n- Passenger wayfinding",
      "examples": [
        "I ",
        "D ",
        "1 ",
        "T3",
        "  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#aircraft_type",
      "name": "aircraft_type",
      "fieldType": "iata_aircraft",
      "position": {
        "start": 72,
        "end": 74,
        "length": 3
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "pattern": "^[A-Z0-9]{3}$",
      "description": "IATA aircraft type code. 3-character code identifying the aircraft model. See SSIM Appendix A.",
      "aiNotes": "Aircraft type. Format: 3-character IATA code.\n\nThe IATA aircraft type code table is maintained separately and updated regularly as new aircraft enter service. The 3-character code fits the existing field — no format change is needed for new types.\n\nCommon examples (including types added post-2011):\n\nWidebody:\n- '388' = Airbus A380-800\n- '789' = Boeing 787-9 Dreamliner\n- '78X' = Boeing 787-10 Dreamliner\n- '77W' = Boeing 777-300ER\n- '779' = Boeing 777-9 (777X family)\n- '359' = Airbus A350-900\n- '351' = Airbus A350-1000\n\nNarrowbody:\n- '73H' = Boeing 737-800\n- '7M8' = Boeing 737 MAX 8\n- '7M9' = Boeing 737 MAX 9\n- '7M7' = Boeing 737 MAX 7\n- '32N' = Airbus A320neo\n- '32Q' = Airbus A321neo\n- '32X' = Airbus A321XLR\n- '32A' = Airbus A320 (classic)\n- '321' = Airbus A321 (classic)\n- '223' = Airbus A220-300\n\nRegional:\n- 'E95' = Embraer E195-E2\n- 'E90' = Embraer E190\n- 'AT7' = ATR 72\n\nFormat:\n- First char: Aircraft family\n- Last 2 chars: Variant/series\n\nUsed for:\n- Capacity planning\n- Passenger information\n- Gate assignment\n- Fuel planning\n- Crew qualification\n\nCritical for:\n- Booking (seat availability)\n- Operations (aircraft capabilities)\n- Maintenance (type-specific requirements)\n\nNote: New codes are added by IATA as new aircraft models enter service. Parsers should not reject unknown 3-character codes — log a warning and pass through.",
      "examples": [
        "388",
        "789",
        "78X",
        "77W",
        "779",
        "359",
        "351",
        "73H",
        "7M8",
        "7M9",
        "32N",
        "32Q",
        "32X",
        "223",
        "E95"
      ],
      "relatesTo": {
        "@type": "FieldRelationship",
        "target": "iata.aircraft_type",
        "relationship": "references_aircraft_type",
        "description": "Links to IATA aircraft type registry"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#passenger_reservations_booking_designator",
      "name": "passenger_reservations_booking_designator",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 75,
        "end": 94,
        "length": 20
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Passenger Reservations Booking Designator (PRBD). Lists available booking classes. Mandatory if aircraft_configuration_version (173-192) is blank. Either this field OR aircraft_configuration_version must be non-blank.",
      "aiNotes": "Booking classes available. Format: 20 characters, left-justified.\n\nExample: 'JCYZWHKMNLSRTQVUOBXE'\n\nEach character = One booking class:\n- J, C = Business class\n- Y, W, H = Full-fare economy\n- K, M, L, S = Discount economy\n- etc.\n\nOrder: Typically highest to lowest fare\n\nUsed for:\n- Booking system integration\n- Inventory management\n- Fare class availability\n- Revenue management\n\nEither PRBD OR aircraft_configuration_version must be present (not both blank).\n\nBlank if using aircraft_configuration_version instead.",
      "examples": [
        "JCYZWHKMNLSRTQVUOBXE",
        "FYB                 ",
        "                    "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#passenger_reservations_booking_modifier",
      "name": "passenger_reservations_booking_modifier",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 95,
        "end": 99,
        "length": 5
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Passenger Reservations Booking Modifier (PRBM). Modifiers for booking classes. Blank-filled by PRBD class. Conditional field.",
      "aiNotes": "Booking class modifiers. Format: 5 characters.\n\nRarely used. Usually blank.\n\nProvides additional restrictions or modifiers to PRBD classes.",
      "examples": [
        "     ",
        "XX   "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#meal_service_note",
      "name": "meal_service_note",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 100,
        "end": 109,
        "length": 10
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "O",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Meal service codes by booking class. Left-justified, blank-padded. Optional field.",
      "aiNotes": "Meal service information. Format: 10 characters.\n\nCodes per booking class:\n- M = Meal\n- S = Snack\n- B = Breakfast\n- L = Lunch\n- D = Dinner\n- R = Refreshment\n\nExample: 'MMMLLLLSSS'\n- First 3 classes (J, C, Y): Full meal (M)\n- Next 4 classes: Lunch (L)\n- Last 3 classes: Snack (S)\n\nOptional. Can be overridden in RT4 records.",
      "examples": [
        "MMMLLLLSSS",
        "BBBDDD    ",
        "          "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#joint_operation_airline_designators",
      "name": "joint_operation_airline_designators",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 110,
        "end": 118,
        "length": 9
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Up to 3 joint operation carrier designators. Packed in 3×3 bytes (111-113, 114-116, 117-119). For 2-character codes, 3rd byte of each slot must be blank. Left-justify and blank-fill if fewer than three carriers.",
      "aiNotes": "Joint operation carriers. Format: 9 characters (3 × 3-char slots)\n\nFor code-share or joint-venture flights.\n\nExample: 'QF BA AA '\n- Slot 1 (111-113): 'QF ' = Qantas\n- Slot 2 (114-116): 'BA ' = British Airways\n- Slot 3 (117-119): 'AA ' = American Airlines\n\nEach airline can sell seats on this flight.\n\nBlank if not a code-share/joint operation.\n\nNote: Each 3-byte slot follows airline_designator format (2-char codes end with blank).",
      "examples": [
        "QF BA AA ",
        "DL AF KL ",
        "         "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#mct_international_domestic_status",
      "name": "mct_international_domestic_status",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 119,
        "end": 120,
        "length": 2
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "O",
      "pattern": "^[DI]{2}$",
      "description": "Minimum Connect Time (MCT) international/domestic status. Two characters: Position 120=departure status, Position 121=arrival status. 'D'=Domestic, 'I'=International.",
      "aiNotes": "Int'l/Domestic status for MCT. Format: 2 characters.\n\nPosition 1 (byte 120): Departure status\nPosition 2 (byte 121): Arrival status\n\nValues:\n- 'D' = Domestic\n- 'I' = International\n\nExamples:\n- 'DD' = Domestic departure → Domestic arrival (domestic flight)\n- 'II' = International departure → International arrival (int'l flight)\n- 'DI' = Domestic departure → International arrival (outbound int'l)\n- 'ID' = International departure → Domestic arrival (inbound int'l)\n\nUsed for:\n- Minimum connect time rules\n- Immigration/customs requirements\n- Terminal assignment",
      "examples": [
        "DD",
        "II",
        "DI",
        "ID",
        "  "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#secure_flight_indicator",
      "name": "secure_flight_indicator",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 121,
        "end": 121,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "O",
      "allowedValues": [
        "S",
        " "
      ],
      "description": "Secure Flight indicator. 'S' if subject to secure flight regulations, blank if not.",
      "aiNotes": "Secure flight indicator.\n\nValues:\n- 'S' = Subject to secure flight requirements\n- ' ' = Not applicable\n\nSecure Flight: US TSA program requiring Advance Passenger Information System (APIS) data submission prior to departure.\n\nUsually 'S' for:\n- Flights departing from or arriving in the USA\n- Flights overflying US airspace (including transiting US airspace without landing)\n- Flights to/from US territories (Guam, Puerto Rico, US Virgin Islands, etc.)\n\nClarifications (post-2011 editions):\n- Expanded guidance on applicability to overflights and technical stops\n- Airlines must indicate Secure Flight status for ALL flights where TSA APIS data is required\n- Codeshare flights: the operating carrier's Secure Flight obligation applies regardless of marketing carrier\n- Similar APIS requirements exist in other jurisdictions (EU API Directive, Canada PAXIS, Australia APP) but are NOT indicated by this field — this field is TSA-specific only\n\nBlank for flights with no US nexus.",
      "examples": [
        "S",
        " "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
