      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#operating_airline_disclosure_marker",
      "name": "operating_airline_disclosure_marker",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 148,
        "end": 148,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "fillRule": "blank",
      "description": "Code-share/wet-lease designation marker (DEI 2/9). Blank if not used. Indicates if flight is operated by a different carrier than the marketing carrier.",
      "aiNotes": "Operating airline disclosure. Code-share indicator.\n\nBlank = airline_designator is operating carrier\nNon-blank = Flight operated by different carrier (code-share)\n\nExample:\nMarketing: AA (American)\nOperating: BA (British Airways)\n→ Code-share flight, marker non-blank",
      "examples": [
        " ",
        "X"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#traffic_restriction_code",
      "name": "traffic_restriction_code",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 149,
        "end": 159,
        "length": 11
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Traffic restriction codes. Left-justified, blank-padded. Indicates restrictions on passenger carriage (e.g., local traffic prohibited, regulatory restrictions).",
      "aiNotes": "Traffic restrictions. Format: 11 characters, left-justified, blank-padded.\n\nStandard restriction codes:\n- 'A' = No local traffic (passengers cannot board/disembark at this point)\n- 'B' = Local traffic only\n- 'C' = Local and behind/beyond traffic only\n- 'D' = Qualify - contact carrier\n- 'E' = No local traffic, behind/beyond permitted\n- 'F'-'Z' = Various restriction combinations per SSIM Chapter 5\n\nRestriction categories:\n- Cabotage prohibitions (domestic carriage by foreign carrier)\n- Fifth freedom restrictions (traffic rights between two foreign countries)\n- Bilateral air service agreement limitations\n- Government-imposed route restrictions\n\nPost-2011 updates:\n- New codes added for EU261/EC261 regulatory compliance scenarios\n- Additional codes for regional passenger rights regulations (e.g., Canadian APPR, Brazilian ANAC)\n- Clarified handling of restriction codes for codeshare flights vs operating carrier flights\n- Overflow indicator (byte 161) used when more than 11 restriction characters needed\n\nBlank if no restrictions apply.\n\nMultiple codes can be concatenated (e.g., 'AE' = no local + no local behind/beyond).",
      "examples": [
        "           ",
        "A          ",
        "AE         "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#traffic_restriction_code_leg_overflow",
      "name": "traffic_restriction_code_leg_overflow",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 160,
        "end": 160,
        "length": 1
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "fillRule": "blank",
      "description": "Traffic restriction code overflow indicator. Blank when not used.",
      "aiNotes": "Traffic restriction overflow. Usually blank.",
      "examples": [
        " "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#spare_3",
      "name": "spare_3",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 161,
        "end": 171,
        "length": 11
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "fillRule": "blank",
      "description": "Reserved field. Must be blank-filled (11 bytes).",
      "aiNotes": "Reserved/spare field. Always 11 blanks.",
      "examples": [
        "           "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#aircraft_configuration_version",
      "name": "aircraft_configuration_version",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 172,
        "end": 191,
        "length": 20
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "C",
      "alignment": "left",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Aircraft configuration/version identifier. Either this field OR passenger_reservations_booking_designator (76-95) must be non-blank. Identifies specific aircraft configuration (seat layout, capacity).",
      "aiNotes": "Aircraft configuration. Format: 20 characters.\n\nAlternative to PRBD for identifying aircraft layout.\n\nExample: 'J8Y174' = 8 Business, 174 Economy seats\n\nEither:\n- Use PRBD (booking classes), OR\n- Use this (configuration)\n\nNot both blank!\n\nTypically:\n- PRBD for booking systems\n- This field for operational planning",
      "examples": [
        "J8Y174              ",
        "F12J32Y180         ",
        "                    "
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#date_variation",
      "name": "date_variation",
      "fieldType": "string",
      "position": {
        "start": 192,
        "end": 193,
        "length": 2
      },
      "required": false,
      "status": "O",
      "alignment": "right",
      "padding": "blank",
      "description": "Date variation indicator. Right-justified, blank-padded. Indicates arrival date offset from departure date (+/- days).",
      "aiNotes": "Arrival date variation. Format: 2 characters, right-justified.\n\nIndicates arrival day relative to departure:\n- '  ' = Same day\n- '+1' = Next day (+1 day)\n- '+2' = Two days later\n- '-1' = Previous day (rare, time zone crossing)\n\nMost long-haul flights: '+1' (arrive next day)\n\nExample:\nDepart SYD: Mon 23:50\nArrive LAX: Mon 14:50 (same calendar day, crosses date line!)\n→ date_variation might be '-1'\n\nOr:\nDepart SYD: Mon 09:00\nArrive LHR: Mon 17:00 (next calendar day)\n→ date_variation = '+1'",
      "examples": [
        "  ",
        "+1",
        "+2",
        "-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Field",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#record_serial_number",
      "name": "record_serial_number",
      "fieldType": "integer",
      "position": {
        "start": 194,
        "end": 199,
        "length": 6
      },
      "required": true,
      "status": "M",
      "format": {
        "zeroPad": 6,
        "radix": 10
      },
      "alignment": "right",
      "padding": "zero",
      "description": "Sequential record number within the file. Right-justified, zero-padded. Increments from previous record regardless of record type.",
      "aiNotes": "Sequential record number. Format: 6-digit zero-padded.\n\nIncrements sequentially through file:\nRT1: 000001\nRT2: 000002\nRT3: 000003 ← This record type\nRT3: 000004\nRT4: 000005\n...\n\nFor RT3: Typically ≥ 3",
      "examples": [
        "000003",
        "000010",
        "000100",
        "001234"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "validations": [
    {
      "@type": "Validation",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#validation_fixed_length",
      "name": "fixed_length",
      "validationType": "length",
      "rule": {
        "equals": 200
      },
      "errorMessage": "Flight Leg record must be exactly 200 bytes",
      "severity": "error"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Validation",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#validation_required_constants",
      "name": "required_constants",
      "validationType": "constant_fields",
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "record_type",
          "value": "3"
        }
      ],
      "errorMessage": "Flight Leg record must have record_type = '3'",
      "severity": "error"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Validation",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#validation_different_stations",
      "name": "different_stations",
      "validationType": "field_inequality",
      "fields": [
        "departure_station",
        "arrival_station"
      ],
      "errorMessage": "departure_station must be different from arrival_station (no zero-length legs)",
      "severity": "error"
    }
  ],
  "semanticRules": [
    {
      "@type": "SemanticRule",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#sr_rt3_dates_within_rt2_window",
      "name": "rt3_dates_within_rt2_window",
      "description": "The RT3 period_of_operation_from/to must lie within the RT2 validity window.",
      "checkType": "external",
      "validationLogic": "Verify RT3 operation period falls within parent RT2 period_of_validity_from/to",
      "errorMessage": "RT3 operation period extends outside RT2 carrier validity window",
      "severity": "error"
    },
    {
      "@type": "SemanticRule",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#sr_prbd_or_config_mandatory",
      "name": "prbd_or_config_mandatory",
      "description": "Either PRBD (76-95) OR Aircraft Configuration/Version (173-192) must be populated (non-blank).",
      "checkType": "external",
      "validationLogic": "At least one of passenger_reservations_booking_designator or aircraft_configuration_version must be non-blank",
      "errorMessage": "Either PRBD or Aircraft Configuration must be specified (both cannot be blank)",
      "severity": "error"
    },
    {
      "@type": "SemanticRule",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#sr_times_compatible_with_time_mode",
      "name": "times_compatible_with_time_mode",
      "description": "All HHMM fields must be parsed using the time mode (U/L) declared in RT2.",
      "checkType": "external",
      "validationLogic": "Interpret all time fields (STD/STA) according to parent RT2 time_mode",
      "errorMessage": "Time interpretation must use RT2 time_mode (UTC or Local)",
      "severity": "warning"
    }
  ],
  "relationships": [
    {
      "@type": "Relationship",
      "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
      "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
      "relationship": "belongs_to",
      "cardinality": "N:1",
      "description": "RT3 belongs to parent RT2 carrier",
      "navigable": true
    },
    {
      "@type": "Relationship",
      "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
      "target": "ssim.ch7.record_type_4",
      "relationship": "has_segments",
      "cardinality": "1:N",
      "description": "RT3 may have zero or more RT4 segment data records",
      "navigable": true
    },
    {
      "@type": "Relationship",
      "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
      "target": "iata.airport",
      "relationship": "departs_from",
      "via": "departure_station",
      "cardinality": "N:1",
      "navigable": true
    },
    {
      "@type": "Relationship",
      "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
      "target": "iata.airport",
      "relationship": "arrives_at",
      "via": "arrival_station",
      "cardinality": "N:1",
      "navigable": true
    },
    {
      "@type": "Relationship",
      "source": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3",
      "target": "iata.aircraft_type",
      "relationship": "operated_by_aircraft",
      "via": "aircraft_type",
      "cardinality": "N:1",
      "navigable": true
    }
  ],
  "extensions": [
    {
      "@type": "Extension",
      "@id": "ssim.ch7.record_type_3#ext_segments",
      "name": "segments",
      "description": "Lazily-loaded collection of Segment Data records (RT4) associated with this flight leg. Each segment provides additional data elements (DEIs) for specific board/off point combinations.",
      "extensionType": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "ssim.ch7.record_type_4"
      },
      "loadingStrategy": "lazy",
      "joinCondition": [
        "rt3.airline_designator = rt4.airline_designator",
        "rt3.flight_number = rt4.flight_number",
        "rt3.itinerary_variation_identifier = rt4.itinerary_variation_identifier",
        "rt3.leg_sequence_number = rt4.leg_sequence_number",
        "rt3.service_type = rt4.service_type"
      ],
      "ordering": "ORDER BY rt4.off_point, rt4.data_element_identifier",
      "notes": [
        "This field is NOT encoded in the 200-byte fixed-width RT3 record",
        "It is populated at the application layer during parsing/API responses",
        "If no RT4 records match, this array will be empty",
        "Segments are ordered by off_point, then DEI number",
        "Multiple segments can exist for the same board/off point with different DEIs"
      ],
      "exampleValue": [
        {
          "data_element_identifier": "106",
          "board_point": "BNE",
          "off_point": "DPS",
          "segment_data": "JCDZYBWHKLREONVPQTISFUMAGX"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "trainingExamples": [
    {
      "@type": "TrainingExample",
      "name": "Brisbane to Bali Flight",
      "input": "3 XX  0450101J07DEC2402FEB251234567 BNE23502350+1000I DPS06000600+0800I 7M8XX                                                                       X                       J8Y174                000003",
      "output": {
        "record_type": "3",
        "airline_designator": "XX ",
        "flight_number": "0450",
        "itinerary_variation_identifier": 1,
        "leg_sequence_number": 1,
        "service_type": "J",
        "period_of_operation_from": "2024-12-07",
        "period_of_operation_to": "2025-02-02",
        "days_of_operation": [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7
        ],
        "departure_station": "BNE",
        "passenger_std": "23:50",
        "aircraft_std": "23:50",
        "departure_utc_variation": "+1000",
        "departure_terminal": "I ",
        "arrival_station": "DPS",
        "aircraft_sta": "06:00",
        "passenger_sta": "06:00",
        "arrival_utc_variation": "+0800",
        "arrival_terminal": "I ",
        "aircraft_type": "7M8",
        "aircraft_configuration_version": "J8Y174",
        "record_serial_number": 3
      },
      "explanation": "Daily flight XX450 Brisbane to Bali. Departs 23:50 local (Brisbane UTC+10), arrives 06:00 local (Bali UTC+8). Aircraft: Boeing 737 MAX 8. Configuration: 8 Business, 174 Economy. Operates daily Dec 7, 2024 - Feb 2, 2025. This is record #3 (first RT3 after RT1/RT2).",
      "encoding": "ASCII"
    }
  ],
  "usageExamples": [],
  "references": [
    {
      "@type": "Reference",
      "title": "IATA SSIM Chapter 7.5.3 - Flight Leg Record (Record Type 3)",
      "version": "March 2011",
      "url": "https://www.iata.org/en/publications/ssim/",
      "description": "Official IATA SSIM specification for Flight Leg Record format"
    }
  ],
  "implementationNotes": [
    "RT3 times inherit time_mode from parent RT2 - CRITICAL for correct interpretation",
    "Either PRBD OR aircraft_configuration_version must be non-blank (validate!)",
    "days_of_operation is applied to aircraft_std to determine operating dates",
    "departure_station must ≠ arrival_station (no zero-length legs)",
    "period_of_operation must fall within parent RT2 validity period",
    "UTC offsets (departure_utc_variation, arrival_utc_variation) critical for time zone conversion",
    "aircraft_type determines capacity and operational capabilities",
    "leg_sequence_number distinguishes multiple legs of same flight number",
    "date_variation indicates arrival date offset (typically +1 for long-haul)",
    "All spare fields must be blank-filled for strict SSIM compliance"
  ],
  "status": "stable",
  "dateCreated": "2025-10-18",
  "dateModified": "2025-10-18",
  "contributors": [
    "Active Flights Specification Team",
    "IATA SSIM Working Group"
  ],
  "license": "https://activeflights.com/licenses/specs-v1",
  "seeAlso": [
    "ssim.ch7.record_type_1",
    "ssim.ch7.record_type_2",
    "ssim.ch7.record_type_4",
    "ssim.ch7.record_type_5"
  ],
  "changelog": [
    {
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "date": "2025-11-24",
      "changes": [
        "Initial release of Flight Leg Record (RT3) specification",
        "Standardized @type to RecordSpecification",
        "Converted field positions from 1-based to 0-based indexing",
        "Added sharedVocabulary reference to shared.vocabulary.jsonld",
        "Added indexing note in conventions section"
      ]
    }
  ]
}